{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00274",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 3.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Good morning, how are you doing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.67,
      "end_seconds": 6.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Weather's turned, hasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.24,
      "end_seconds": 12.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Um, it has. I got caught in the rain walking over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.54,
      "end_seconds": 15.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "How can I help you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.45,
      "end_seconds": 30.19,
      "duration_seconds": 13.74,
      "text": "Yeah, I'm here because of red scaly patches on my elbows. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.6,
      "end_seconds": 38.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.52,
      "end_seconds": 49.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "Well, uh, I notice it more with stress and cold weather. I'd give it a four, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.21,
      "end_seconds": 52.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.96,
      "end_seconds": 79.51,
      "duration_seconds": 25.55,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get scaling on the scalp as well. The scaling on the scalp? That's been for about a year. With scaling on the scalp, about a seven out of ten. Oh, and itching. Yeah, you know, as for itching, maybe a three out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.6,
      "end_seconds": 83.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.47,
      "end_seconds": 92.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "So, uh, just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.64,
      "end_seconds": 98.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Alright, any weeping, eye redness or new medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.29,
      "end_seconds": 105.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "No weeping, eye redness or new medicines, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.26,
      "end_seconds": 109.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Any fever or sore throat before it started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.62,
      "end_seconds": 111.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.3,
      "end_seconds": 115.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.85,
      "end_seconds": 121.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Okay, so yes, ibuprofen, it gives me stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.42,
      "end_seconds": 127.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.95,
      "end_seconds": 133.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "So, yes, I had a hernia repair, about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.91,
      "end_seconds": 138.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.15,
      "end_seconds": 151.72,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Yeah, not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.36,
      "end_seconds": 158.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.34,
      "end_seconds": 161.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.29,
      "end_seconds": 165.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Okay, are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.73,
      "end_seconds": 170.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Metformin. I take it 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.57,
      "end_seconds": 174.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.65,
      "end_seconds": 179.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Yeah, no, it's at home. Coconut oil, daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.54,
      "end_seconds": 181.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.34,
      "end_seconds": 184.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.93,
      "end_seconds": 186.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.87,
      "end_seconds": 198.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.69,
      "end_seconds": 216.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.7 degrees, heart rate 72, blood pressure 121 over 73, oxygen saturation is 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.29,
      "end_seconds": 218.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.07,
      "end_seconds": 235.8,
      "duration_seconds": 16.73,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.39,
      "end_seconds": 238.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.7,
      "end_seconds": 243.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.91,
      "end_seconds": 246.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.24,
      "end_seconds": 260.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "A few small pits in the fingernails."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.2,
      "end_seconds": 285.26,
      "duration_seconds": 21.06,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with plaque psoriasis at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.76,
      "end_seconds": 289.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Doctor, uh, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.85,
      "end_seconds": 305.98,
      "duration_seconds": 16.13,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like plaque psoriasis, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had red scaly patches on your elbows, and no sore throat before it started or eye redness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.27,
      "end_seconds": 308.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.1,
      "end_seconds": 313.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.46,
      "end_seconds": 328.01,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "Right, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.49,
      "end_seconds": 336.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for baseline before treatment. I'll start you on calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day, for four weeks. It's for psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.82,
      "end_seconds": 339.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.27,
      "end_seconds": 349.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "A little sunlight helps psoriasis, but avoid sunburn. Moisturise often. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. We'll refer you to a dermatologist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.37,
      "end_seconds": 355.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.1,
      "end_seconds": 364.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.61,
      "end_seconds": 368.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Okay, um, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.76,
      "end_seconds": 384.66,
      "duration_seconds": 15.9,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in four weeks. Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.68,
      "end_seconds": 397.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "So, I take the calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.16,
      "end_seconds": 402.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.97,
      "end_seconds": 405.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Yeah, no questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.87,
      "end_seconds": 408.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Alright, take care."
    }
  ]
}